(7445477, 1177565, 86447, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Christophe and Daddy Christophe!<br/> <br/>I believe that there''s no reason not to laugh... genuinely laugh... a bunch, though.  :D<br/> <br/>I also love silence.   We recently had a worker who was here for months every day.   He commented, "It''s so quiet here."<br/> <br/>I told him that if he could figure out how to turn on the TV (I don''t know how), he was welcome to it, but that I enjoy silence.<br/> <br/>I also enjoy laughing.  :D<br/> <br/>Sometimes my laughter is the only thing I hear all day until Hubby gets home.   <br/> <br/>I like that.</td>', 'Congratulations, Christophe and Daddy Christophe! I believe that there''s no reason not to laugh... genuinely laugh... a bunch, though.  :D I also love silence.   We recently had a worker who was here for months every day.   He commented, "It''s so quiet here." I told him that if he could figure out how to turn on the TV (I don''t know how), he was welcome to it, but that I enjoy silence. I also enjoy laughing.  :D Sometimes my laughter is the only thing I hear all day until Hubby gets home.    I like that.', '2016-03-22 18:50:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7445478, 1177584, 86447, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  I gave your son a 12... but you only got a 9.  :D<br/></td>', 'Congratulations!  I gave your son a 12... but you only got a 9.  :D', '2016-03-22 18:51:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7445480, 1176937, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes to the challenge well<br/> <br/>A competent shot of a heron doing what herons do, I find myself captivated by trying to determine what he has in his beak and if the red object immediately behind and below his beak is part of that same unfortunate victim. He stands out well from the soft focus background and so I have to disagree with some of the comments about softness and standing out from the background, the eye is pin sharp and thats what matters. Thanks for the processing details, all very involved by the sound of it and I would say it has generally paid off<br/> <br/>Thanks for your entry Alice</td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An interesting image that contributes to the challenge well A competent shot of a heron doing what herons do, I find myself captivated by trying to determine what he has in his beak and if the red object immediately behind and below his beak is part of that same unfortunate victim. He stands out well from the soft focus background and so I have to disagree with some of the comments about softness and standing out from the background, the eye is pin sharp and thats what matters. Thanks for the processing details, all very involved by the sound of it and I would say it has generally paid off Thanks for your entry Alice', '2016-03-22 18:54:03.000000', NULL, 0),
